  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A crossbow stock fitted with a coil of copper where the bow should be. The coil crackles in dry weather, and compasses carried near it point at it and nowhere else.</p><p>You have a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.</p><p>This launcher needs no ammunition: it throws bolts of lightning, and its attacks deal Lightning damage instead of Piercing damage.</p><p><strong>Discharge.</strong> As an action, you discharge the coil in a Line 120 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in it makes a [[/save ability=dex dc=20 format=long]], taking [[/damage 10d8 type=lightning]] damage on a failed save or half as much on a success. The coil holds three discharges and winds itself full again at dawn.</p><p><strong>It Wants a Storm.</strong> Left pointing at the sky in a thunderstorm, the launcher drinks a lightning strike and keeps it. Its owner can let that one strike go again later, anywhere, as nothing more than light and noise: enough to be seen and heard for ten miles.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
